@startuml 07_state_async_bus
!include _style.iuml

title ExpanderPort transfer engine - bare-metal asynchronous mode (UML state machine)

[*] --> Uninitialised
Uninitialised --> ApplyFailSafe : init()
ApplyFailSafe : write OUTPUT = fail_safe levels
ApplyFailSafe : then CONFIG (direction)
ApplyFailSafe : order prevents output glitch
ApplyFailSafe --> Idle : ok
ApplyFailSafe --> Recovery : bus error

Idle : shadow == hardware
Idle --> Pending : write_masked() [main context]\n/ shadow_out, dirty |= mask

Pending : changes merged in shadow
Pending --> Pending : write_masked()\n(coalesced, no extra transfer)
Pending --> Transferring : poll()\n[bus idle] / snapshot = shadow_out;\ndirty = 0; start non-blocking transfer

Transferring : LPI2C non-blocking transfer in progress
Transferring --> Transferring : write_masked() [main context]\n/ shadow_out, dirty |= mask
Transferring --> Completed : completion ISR [status OK]\n/ xfer_status.store(Done)
Transferring --> Recovery : completion ISR [NACK | timeout]\n/ xfer_status.store(Error)

Completed --> Idle : poll() [dirty == 0]
Completed --> Transferring : poll() [dirty != 0]\n/ new snapshot

Recovery : bus recover(): 9 SCL clocks + STOP
Recovery : retries < cfg.max_retries
Recovery --> Resync : recovered
Recovery --> Faulted : retries exhausted

Resync : read OUTPUT + CONFIG back
Resync : chip reset detected -> ApplyFailSafe
Resync --> Pending : ok (dirty = all written bits)
Resync --> ApplyFailSafe : reset detected

Faulted : port reports Error::Io on every call
Faulted : application decides (degrade / reset)
Faulted --> Recovery : reset_port() by application

note right of Transferring
  Shared-state ownership (bare-metal):
  - shadow_out, dirty: main context only
    (write_masked, poll) -> no lock needed.
  - xfer_status: written by completion ISR,
    read by poll(); std::atomic<uint8_t>
    store/load only -> lock-free on every
    Cortex-M, including M0+.
  Only poll() starts transfers; the ISR never
  chains a transfer and never touches the shadow.
  Expander writes from ISR are rejected
  (Error::IsrContext).
end note
@enduml
